Four of the read_file calls here are supposed to fault, and each one is taken
by a barrier -- that is the subject of the file. A taken catch longjmps past C
frames whose references nothing can release, so leak detection is off for it;
see the header of run.sh. What the raise itself owns is released before it
raises: `io_read_file` frees the slurped buffer first, checked with leak
detection on over an 800 KB malformed file read eight times (50 bytes leaked,
in one allocation, none of it the buffer).
